1
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:47,759
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,940
[Episode 13]

3
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:58,150
This young man

4
00:01:58,350 --> 00:01:59,750
got hit by a car!

5
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:00,640
Are you okay?

6
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,000
Look how badly you hit him!

7
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,350
He must be seriously injured somewhere.

8
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:06,310
How much will you have to pay for this?

9
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:06,840
Zhou Ke.

10
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:08,210
Is that Zhou Ke?

11
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:11,540
Zhou...

12
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,080
You, sit up.

13
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,010
Look at me properly and see who I am.

14
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,430
Mr. Yu.

15
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:18,600
Mr. Yu?

16
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:19,690
My acting teacher.

17
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,120
Northern Film Academy's

18
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,840
outstanding student
of the 2012 acting cohort.

19
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,430
The lead actor in my graduation play.

20
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:26,120
The idol of the whole school.

21
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:27,310
And you were faking a car accident?

22
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:28,070
Mr. Yu, I...

23
00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:29,070
Acting like this?

24
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:32,280
Mr. Yu, well,

25
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:33,960
my situation

26
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,240
is quite complicated.

27
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,500
It's not complicated.

28
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:38,120
What's so complicated about it?

29
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:38,680
It is.

30
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,460
Do it again.

31
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,150
With acting like this,

32
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:42,480
no one would let it pass.

33
00:02:42,590 --> 00:02:44,310
How do you know people upstairs

34
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:45,570
wouldn't be watching?

35
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,190
Can you get away with this kind of acting?

36
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:47,850
No, I can't.

37
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:48,680
Let me tell you,

38
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,800
the audience aren't fools.

39
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,120
Fake acting can't fool anyone.

40
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,250
Come on, do it again.

41
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:53,560
Good thing I ran into you.

42
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,220
Okay. Okay.

43
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:54,840
Come on.

44
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,300
Where should I start from?

45
00:02:56,770 --> 00:02:59,030
Start from the preparation in your heart.

46
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:00,520
Don't you know it in your heart?

47
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,000
I got it.

48
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:01,800
Come on.

49
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:03,240
Wait, what are you doing?

50
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,960
You still listen to him
after graduating so many years ago?

51
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,870
He was the first to invest in my movie,

52
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:07,870
and he didn't even ask us to pay it back.

53
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:09,190
Mr. Yu, let me find you a seat.

54
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:09,750
You can sit and watch.

55
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:10,680
No need. No need.

56
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:11,540
Just stay here.

57
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:12,710
You can be the audience.

58
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:13,240
Go ahead.

59
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:14,680
Ready.

60
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:16,310
What kind of acting was that?

61
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:17,490
Action.

62
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:19,400
Oh my god.

63
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,410
Is this okay, Mr. Yu?

64
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,960
Do you think it's right?

65
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,470
Not quite.

66
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:25,240
Then do it again.

67
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:25,570
Okay.

68
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:26,640
Ready.

69
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,560
Do you think it works?

70
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:32,290
Pretty good.

71
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,000
Is it?

72
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:33,770
Not good.

73
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:34,680
Where is your confidence?

74
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,240
It's pretty good.

75
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:35,770
It's bad.

76
00:03:36,070 --> 00:03:37,150
Is it good or bad?

77
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:38,710
Would I say anything if it was good?

78
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:39,710
Then what's the problem?

79
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:41,510
Do you know where the problem is?

80
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:44,310
You've given everything

81
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:45,750
I taught you back to me.

82
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:47,079
-You only played the result.
-Yes.

83
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:48,560
You didn't act out the process.

84
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,650
-Yes.
-Where is your psychological process?

85
00:03:49,650 --> 00:03:50,000
Gone.

86
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:51,680
Why did you fake an accident?

87
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:52,430
Behind you.

88
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:54,150
What's the most important thing
in acting, you know?

89
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:55,190
It's having a sincere heart.

90
00:03:55,190 --> 00:03:56,000
Yes, Mr. Yu.

91
00:03:56,210 --> 00:03:57,030
Why did you fake an accident?

92
00:03:57,030 --> 00:03:57,630
There's a car coming from behind.

93
00:03:57,630 --> 00:03:58,360
Why fake an accident?

94
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:58,710
Because...

95
00:03:58,710 --> 00:03:59,710
Are you in trouble?

96
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:00,120
Definitely.

97
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,280
I didn't see your pain.

98
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:01,960
-Yes, Mr. Yu.
-A car is coming.

99
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,030
Don't worry about it.

100
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:04,190
You need to concentrate right now.

101
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:04,520
Okay.

102
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:05,320
Listen to me.

103
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:06,280
You are now

104
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,680
a typical character
in an atypical environment.

105
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,080
Right?

106
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,250
According to our grandmaster,

107
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:12,470
Stanislavski,

108
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:14,760
you need to go from the outside in,

109
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:16,160
and then from the inside out.

110
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:16,829
Mr. Yu, why don't you

111
00:04:16,829 --> 00:04:18,040
move the car out first?

112
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,390
Hey, who is it?

113
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:21,630
Why are you blocking the way here?

114
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:23,160
My motorcade can't get out.

115
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:25,370
Lei Ou.

116
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,590
Zhou Ke.

117
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,870
Do you know how long
I've been looking for you?

118
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:29,720
Lei Ou,

119
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,720
about the money we owe you,

120
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,430
if you give us a few more days,

121
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:33,310
we can definitely pay it back.

122
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:33,830
Lei Ou?

123
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:36,120
M-Mr. Yu.

124
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:38,040
You still remember me?

125
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:38,750
How could I forget?

126
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:39,630
Your name, Lei Ou.

127
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:41,390
The whole school knew Lei Ou.

128
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,190
How could I forget?

129
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:43,390
It's very memorable.

130
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:44,790
Mr. Yu. You're my senior?

131
00:04:46,350 --> 00:04:47,680
Otherwise, would I have lent you money?

132
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,600
Yes, Mr. Yu. I only did this

133
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,630
-to pay him back.
-Yes.

134
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:51,070
What are you

135
00:04:51,070 --> 00:04:51,750
doing here?

136
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,270
I...

137
00:04:53,270 --> 00:04:55,270
-He mainly lends money.
-Lends money.

138
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:55,870
Mr. Yu.

139
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,070
I'm the vehicle manager now,

140
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,150
managing the motorcade.

141
00:04:59,150 --> 00:05:00,240
So after giving out loans,

142
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,900
you manage the motorcade now?

143
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,920
One is an outstanding student
from the 2008 acting cohort

144
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,560
of Northern Film Academy.

145
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:09,310
The other is an outstanding student
from the 2012 acting cohort.

146
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:10,120
You two,

147
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:14,070
one giving out loans
and managing vehicles,

148
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:15,870
and the other faking accidents.

149
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,870
And what kind of acting was that?

150
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,940
Was it even watchable?

151
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:22,560
Where is the acting
you love in your hearts?

152
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,220
Forgotten?

153
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:23,950
Lost?

154
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:26,050
Come on, Lei Ou.

155
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,120
As his senior, show him how it's done.

156
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:30,070
Just the fake accident from earlier.

157
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:30,530
Come on.

158
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:33,120
I don't think that's a good idea, Mr. Yu.

159
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:34,909
Again.

160
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:36,920
I can tell by the sound.

161
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,520
Understood, Mr. Yu. Come on.

162
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:42,750
Make some noise. Come on.

163
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:43,630
I'll join you.

164
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:45,950
Oh my god.

165
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,630
-Mr. Yu.
-Is this okay?

166
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,850
He even hit his head.

167
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,480
You should have the feeling now.

168
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,510
Because I saw your sincerity

169
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:56,800
and hard work.

170
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:59,830
Acting must be sincere

171
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,490
and come from the heart.

172
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:03,630
It's not about fooling around.

173
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:04,630
I invested in your movie.

174
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:05,430
No matter what the result is,

175
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:06,430
I won't regret it.

176
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:09,430
As long as you don't give up on

177
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:10,990
your passion,

178
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:12,720
it's all worth it for me.

179
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:13,560
Okay?

180
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:15,310
If you want to act well,

181
00:06:15,310 --> 00:06:16,310
you must be a good person first.

182
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,310
Acting reflects the person.

183
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:18,370
Never forget this.

184
00:06:19,190 --> 00:06:19,600
Okay?

185
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,050
Okay.

186
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:23,120
Mr. Yu, I'm so touched.

187
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,650
I feel I've benefited a lot.

188
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:26,070
Don't worry, I promise

189
00:06:26,070 --> 00:06:27,120
we will never do such

190
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,310
illegal things again.

191
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:28,710
Right.

192
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:31,120
I'm just a little curious.

193
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:31,480
Tell me.

194
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,190
Because I just bumped into it too.

195
00:06:33,190 --> 00:06:34,280
I was wondering

196
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:37,650
how we can make it look real

197
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:40,430
while protecting ourselves
from getting hurt.

198
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,120
Look, she's eager to learn.

199
00:06:42,659 --> 00:06:43,920
That's a very good question.

200
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,510
-Thank you, Mr. Yu.
-Let me tell you,

201
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:45,920
it's a technical matter.

202
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:48,050
Let me show you.

203
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:51,200
You can't just bump into it foolishly.

204
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:52,770
There's a technique to it.

205
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:53,720
Acting requires sincerity,

206
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,750
but you must protect yourself.

207
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:56,870
Look, it's turning left
with the signal on, right?

208
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:57,720
When you bump into it,

209
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:58,560
you can't come this way,

210
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,680
or it will run you over.

211
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,560
You have to go with it.

212
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,070
You do it like this

213
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:03,070
and move along
with the car after the bump.

214
00:07:03,070 --> 00:07:04,070
Look. Look, look.

215
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,160
Got it?

216
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:07,160
-You need to be sincere.
-Sir.

217
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:07,800
But you also need to protect—

218
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,360
I've already woken up from my nap.

219
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,490
If you can't do it,
I'll get another driver!

220
00:07:11,490 --> 00:07:12,440
Right away. Right away.

221
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,800
I ran into some acquaintances.

222
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:14,930
Sorry. I'm so sorry.

223
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,270
Alright, let's stop here for today.

224
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,560
Mr. Yu, are you...

225
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,290
Experiencing life.

226
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,320
Remember,

227
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,160
never forget to observe

228
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,040
and experience life.

229
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:25,500
I'm off.

230
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,040
Goodbye, Mr. Yu.

231
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:27,600
Goodbye, Mr. Yu.

232
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,680
Thank you, Mr. Yu.

233
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:37,310
Mr. Yu is still so stubborn.

234
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:40,320
Yeah, he hasn't changed at all
after all these years.

235
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,970
He never taught me,

236
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,920
but why am I so touched?

237
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:46,290
Good thing we ran into him.

238
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,720
Lei Ou, I didn't expect

239
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,850
you to be in the acting department too.

240
00:07:52,150 --> 00:07:53,000
What do you mean?

241
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,310
You can't tell from my looks?

242
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,150
No, this...

243
00:07:56,150 --> 00:07:58,310
Since we're fellow students,

244
00:07:58,430 --> 00:07:59,800
can you give us a little more time?

245
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,120
Look, I've already gone down this path.

246
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,240
-Thank god I met Mr. Yu.
-That's right.

247
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:02,950
Give us a few more days.

248
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:03,830
We'll get the money together.

249
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,270
You didn't answer my calls.

250
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:06,600
-Yes.
-You didn't reply to my messages.

251
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,190
I was trying to figure something out.

252
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:07,800
I came to find you

253
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,120
just to tell you this.

254
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,650
The money has been paid off.

255
00:08:11,510 --> 00:08:12,120
Paid off?

256
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,160
Who paid it?

257
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:16,370
That manly guy with the mustache.

258
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,560
You didn't really sell
the convenience store, did you?

259
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,090
I didn't.

260
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:26,920
Then...

261
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:28,410
It wasn't me.

262
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:29,580
Then who was it?

263
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,560
Stop asking.

264
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,030
Tell me.

265
00:08:33,030 --> 00:08:35,030
At a time like this, you're still...

266
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:36,169
Tell me now.

267
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:39,720
How about this?
You don't have to shave anymore.

268
00:08:39,789 --> 00:08:41,549
You can keep
that little toothbrush moustache.

269
00:08:41,549 --> 00:08:42,720
Tell me. Alright?

270
00:08:43,549 --> 00:08:45,270
Good boy, tell me.

271
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,840
Chen Junnan,
are you going to tell me or not?

272
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,790
Ximei, this...

273
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:49,320
Three.

274
00:08:49,670 --> 00:08:49,960
I...

275
00:08:50,550 --> 00:08:51,080
Two.

276
00:08:51,190 --> 00:08:51,630
Zhen.

277
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,580
She told me not to tell you.

278
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:02,810
I'm hanging up now.

279
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:03,320
I...

280
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,060
Is that really necessary?

281
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,550
No, I mean, for our sake,

282
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:10,080
he didn't have to sell the store.

283
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:12,140
This is too much. You should hurry...

284
00:09:12,390 --> 00:09:13,790
He didn't sell the store.

285
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,660
Then how did he pay it back?

286
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,720
Someone else did.

287
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:22,870
Who?

288
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,240
Zhen.

289
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:29,470
She said it was a dividend,

290
00:09:29,550 --> 00:09:31,510
but how long has
Shapu Village been operating?

291
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:33,370
How could she come up with 80,000?

292
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,910
Our portions have gotten so much smaller.

293
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:55,120
Where are you going?

294
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,120
No buying snacks.

295
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,060
I'm going to the bathroom.

296
00:09:58,150 --> 00:09:59,960
Don't use the one at home.
It wastes water.

297
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,780
Go to the village committee later,

298
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:02,870
and wash these bowls while you're at it,

299
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:03,630
and yesterday's too.

300
00:10:03,630 --> 00:10:05,360
Public money is still money.

301
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:07,780
I can't lack this bit of awareness.

302
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:09,840
It's fine.

303
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,440
I'll hold it a bit longer.

304
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,570
When the time comes,

305
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,440
if I can't hold it,
I'll do it all at once.

306
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,570
Then go into the sea.

307
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:18,220
The boat is gone. How can I
go into the sea?

308
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:25,710
Speaking of the boat,

309
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:28,600
I really think my sister

310
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,320
is such a kind

311
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:32,090
and kind

312
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,510
girl.

313
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,510
I didn't expect that someone
who always put money first

314
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:36,670
and her brother second

315
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:39,000
would actually sell the boat for Mr. Zhou.

316
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:42,120
I didn't do it entirely for him.

317
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:45,080
With the remaining money,
can't we still invest in a guesthouse

318
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,480
and open a fish ball shop?

319
00:10:46,910 --> 00:10:49,170
Although we have to
cut back a bit for now,

320
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:51,960
things will definitely
get better for us in the future,

321
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,760
and the shop will get better too.

322
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:54,420
Right.

323
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:56,890
You have vision.

324
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,570
We must have vision.

325
00:10:58,750 --> 00:10:59,610
Think about it.

326
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:01,510
Before Mr. Zhou came,

327
00:11:01,510 --> 00:11:03,080
what kind of life did we live?

328
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,550
Right?

329
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:04,820
Every morning,

330
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,540
we'd just eat some shrimp,

331
00:11:06,870 --> 00:11:07,800
some fish balls,

332
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:11,030
and sometimes even some ribs.

333
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,200
I want to eat ribs.

334
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,700
But we have to look further ahead,

335
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:20,480
right?

336
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,800
We have to look ahead.

337
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:24,080
I believe that after Mr. Zhou
makes his movie

338
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,740
and earns money,
he will definitely pay us back.

339
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:29,490
H-He will definitely pay us back.

340
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:33,910
I'm full.

341
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:34,670
You eat.

342
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,720
-I'm going for a walk.
-You're at home.

343
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,180
Junnan.

344
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:38,770
I brought some things.

345
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,270
W-What do you mean?

346
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,440
Well, I haven't been much help,

347
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:47,510
so from now on,
I'll cover all your food, drinks,

348
00:11:47,510 --> 00:11:49,120
and daily necessities.

349
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:50,970
Since when are you so kind?

350
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,340
Isn't it because Xi...

351
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,430
I'm thoughtful?

352
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,780
They're not expired.

353
00:11:58,870 --> 00:12:01,070
What are you saying? They just arrived.

354
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,360
You're so nice!

355
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,400
It's fine.

356
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,330
We don't lack anything at home.

357
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,270
It's what I should do.

358
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,000
Chen Junnan.

359
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,030
About me selling the boat,

360
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:14,160
you absolutely must not tell Mr. Zhou.

361
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:17,970
Understood.

362
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:18,670
Don't just stand there.

363
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:20,120
We're eating. Join us.

364
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,170
Okay. Let me see.

365
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,480
Never mind. You guys eat.

366
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,630
I'm meeting a friend.

367
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:29,290
We're going

368
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,790
to have brunch.

369
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:32,260
W-What is brunch?

370
00:12:33,030 --> 00:12:33,600
I've never had it.

371
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:35,260
Why don't you take us with you?

372
00:12:37,270 --> 00:12:38,440
No, you can't. You can't.

373
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,840
You two eat together.

374
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:40,790
Who says we can't?

375
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:42,030
Who says? This...

376
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:43,440
Just tell them.

377
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:44,630
Brother! Brother!

378
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:46,220
Why can't we? Take us!

379
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,510
Wait, you haven't taken the bowl yet!

380
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:48,840
The one from last night!

381
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:11,240
You're back.

382
00:13:14,910 --> 00:13:16,230
You're not asleep yet?

383
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:18,610
Who sleeps in the morning?

384
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,630
S-Sometimes I do.

385
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:28,030
Yeah.

386
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:30,580
Have you eaten?

387
00:13:30,790 --> 00:13:31,240
I have.

388
00:13:33,390 --> 00:13:34,250
Are you hungry?

389
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:37,800
If you have nothing to say,
you don't have to force it.

390
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,200
Why did you come back?

391
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,670
I feel like

392
00:13:46,270 --> 00:13:47,270
our relationship

393
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,440
is different now.

394
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:54,030
What is our relationship?

395
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:04,990
Creditor and debtor.

396
00:14:08,150 --> 00:14:09,840
Y-You paid off my debt.

397
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,440
I really appreciate it.

398
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,910
They were pressing hard back then.

399
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:15,110
Thanks for helping me pay it off, but...

400
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:17,000
you even sold the boat for this.

401
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,030
For me.

402
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:19,990
Chen Junnan told you?

403
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:22,650
Was it a secret?

404
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:25,720
You...

405
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,350
Don't overthink it.

406
00:14:27,350 --> 00:14:29,120
Selling the boat
wasn't because of you at all.

407
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,840
It was because I wanted
to open a guesthouse

408
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,040
and was short on cash.

409
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,270
I had a little extra,

410
00:14:33,270 --> 00:14:34,530
so I paid off your debt.

411
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:36,750
It wasn't for you.

412
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,440
I know.

413
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,360
Definitely not.

414
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:47,560
So I came back this time
to pay off my debt.

415
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:52,390
And how do you plan to do that?

416
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:55,930
By working for you.

417
00:14:58,750 --> 00:15:00,150
Then go clean the toilet.

418
00:15:00,910 --> 00:15:02,040
Reporting for duty!

419
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:22,070
Morning.

420
00:15:22,090 --> 00:15:22,690
Morning.

421
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:28,190
You eat.

422
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:28,970
I'll eat.

423
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,930
What do you mean?

424
00:15:47,150 --> 00:15:48,080
Are you eloping?

425
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,150
Did you play tricks on me again?

426
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:50,910
I didn't.

427
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:52,550
Stay out of it.

428
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:55,780
Careful.

429
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:57,750
Are you two together?

430
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:58,380
No.

431
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,280
Then why are you living with him?

432
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:02,190
He has a spare room in his house.

433
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:03,840
He lives in one, and I live in the other.

434
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,840
Is there a problem?

435
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,080
I...

436
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:05,880
And secondly.

437
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,360
If I leave,

438
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:09,750
won't you and Zhen

439
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,200
have more chances to be alone?

440
00:16:12,630 --> 00:16:14,090
Do I have to teach you this?

441
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,360
Why are you looking at me?

442
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,100
Look at the fish balls.

443
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:44,190
-Squeeze.
-Squeeze.

444
00:16:44,190 --> 00:16:45,320
-A spoon.
-A spoon.

445
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:46,670
Scoop.

446
00:16:46,810 --> 00:16:48,090
Scoop. Put it in.

447
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:04,960
Awesome. How did you do that?

448
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:06,609
I'll teach you.

449
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:07,560
Like this.

450
00:17:07,950 --> 00:17:09,550
Unite your waist and stance.

451
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,730
The photos I took of you today
are pretty nice.

452
00:17:26,829 --> 00:17:29,090
They're suitable for a profile picture.

453
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:33,380
They are nice,

454
00:17:33,850 --> 00:17:36,450
but not really suitable
for a profile picture.

455
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:51,200
Why wasn't it approved?

456
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:55,940
[Filming Location of "King of Comedy"]

457
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:58,230
[Crooked Tree]

458
00:17:57,750 --> 00:17:59,310
The number of tourists
has decreased recently.

459
00:17:59,310 --> 00:18:00,710
I wonder what's going on.

460
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:03,590
Indeed, I noticed that too.

461
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:05,650
And it seems like a sudden drop.

462
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:07,970
Is it the off-season recently?

463
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,640
It wasn't the peak season before either.

464
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,550
Is it because our service
is bad somewhere,

465
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,750
giving them a poor experience,

466
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:16,080
so they stopped coming?

467
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,750
Not necessarily.

468
00:18:17,990 --> 00:18:19,390
We're doing pretty well.

469
00:18:19,830 --> 00:18:20,960
But I've actually been thinking recently

470
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,110
that we should do some upgrades.

471
00:18:23,110 --> 00:18:24,480
Since we're using

472
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:25,400
the "King of Comedy"

473
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,240
IP,

474
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:27,110
let's hype it up.

475
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:27,750
We should try

476
00:18:27,750 --> 00:18:28,790
to expand the use

477
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:30,070
of the "King of Comedy" elements

478
00:18:30,070 --> 00:18:31,480
and make them more obvious.

479
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,350
I've thought of a three-step plan.

480
00:18:33,350 --> 00:18:33,830
Step one,

481
00:18:33,830 --> 00:18:36,000
we can set up a big sign by the sea

482
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,070
that says "Work harder! Keep on!"

483
00:18:37,070 --> 00:18:38,400
People can take photos there
facing the sea.

484
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,110
Wouldn't that become a photo spot?

485
00:18:40,110 --> 00:18:40,790
Step two,

486
00:18:40,790 --> 00:18:42,070
under that tree,

487
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:43,480
we make 2 cardboard cutouts

488
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,030
of Stephen Chow and Liu Piaopiao,

489
00:18:45,030 --> 00:18:46,240
leaving the faces blank for tourists.

490
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,830
Wouldn't that be another photo spot?

491
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:49,070
The third one is very important.

492
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:50,310
It will cost some money.

493
00:18:50,310 --> 00:18:52,640
We find some Stephen Chow impersonators.

494
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:56,030
Then they dress up as classic characters
from his movies

495
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,760
and take photos with tourists.

496
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:01,240
The acting village chief
has really improved.

497
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,350
That's a great idea.

498
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:04,150
Are you talking about this kind?

499
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,200
Hometown of "King of Comedy."

500
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:11,020
Chuanao Village?

501
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,870
[Hometown of "King of Comedy"]

502
00:19:12,870 --> 00:19:14,710
[Entering the filming location
of the King of Comedy]

503
00:19:14,790 --> 00:19:18,240
Welcome to
the hometown of "King of Comedy"!

504
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:19,880
Very good!

505
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:21,480
Yours is a little off.

506
00:19:21,510 --> 00:19:23,790
Let me tell you,
when the tourists come later,

507
00:19:23,790 --> 00:19:25,680
show 120% of your enthusiasm.

508
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,850
Take those who want to take photos
to the scenic spots.

509
00:19:27,850 --> 00:19:29,160
Take those who want accommodation
to the hotels.

510
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,090
Take them to restaurants for food.

511
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,880
Stop the bus!

512
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,340
What are you doing? Isn't it dangerous?

513
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:39,270
This is on this main road. Hurry up—

514
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:42,000
Bro, judging by your accent,
you're from Beijing.

515
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,200
Stop imitating the Beijing dialect.

516
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,070
You're finally here.

517
00:19:44,070 --> 00:19:45,510
Going to the hometown
of "King of Comedy," right?

518
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:46,310
Yes.

519
00:19:46,550 --> 00:19:47,590
It's Shapu Village,

520
00:19:47,590 --> 00:19:48,960
the hometown of "King of Comedy." We...

521
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,310
You guys are going too, right?

522
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:51,030
I have two seats left here.

523
00:19:51,030 --> 00:19:51,640
I'll give you a discount.

524
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,000
No.

525
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:52,880
-You two take the bus behind.
-No, no.

526
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,350
-There's another one behind.
-Listen to me.

527
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:55,640
It's a misunderstanding.

528
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:56,680
Shapu Village

529
00:19:56,790 --> 00:19:58,000
is imitating our village.

530
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,920
Chuanao Village, the hometown
of "King of Comedy,"

531
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,480
is the authentic one. Look at our place.

532
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:02,400
Don't talk nonsense.

533
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,750
I have all the itineraries arranged.

534
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:05,270
We are going to Shapu Village.

535
00:20:05,270 --> 00:20:06,030
Their Sha...

536
00:20:06,030 --> 00:20:07,090
What are you doing?

537
00:20:10,350 --> 00:20:11,550
Hold this. Hold this.

538
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,940
What are you doing?

539
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:16,000
I am a proper tour guide.

540
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:19,730
Chuanao Village is the real hometown
of "King of Comedy"!

541
00:20:19,730 --> 00:20:22,380
Folks, we are home!

542
00:20:22,410 --> 00:20:25,000
Welcome to
the hometown of "King of Comedy"!

543
00:20:25,030 --> 00:20:26,400
Come on, let's keep it orderly!

544
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:27,930
Come on, welcome, welcome!

545
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,200
This is our village's bus, right?

546
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:31,640
Yes.

547
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:32,790
Wait a minute!

548
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:33,510
You can't leave! Stop the bus!

549
00:20:33,510 --> 00:20:34,510
Stop, stop, stop!

550
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:36,050
What are you guys doing?

551
00:20:37,590 --> 00:20:39,190
I'll handle this. It's fine.

552
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,270
Up there, here.

553
00:20:48,350 --> 00:20:49,410
Is it appropriate?

554
00:20:49,510 --> 00:20:51,110
Is it appropriate to do this?

555
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:53,880
I was wondering where...

556
00:20:54,350 --> 00:20:56,350
all these distinguished guests...

557
00:20:58,310 --> 00:21:01,480
we worked so hard to invite went.

558
00:21:02,310 --> 00:21:04,240
You intercepted them all halfway.

559
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:06,680
Who are you?

560
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:08,660
You don't even know me?

561
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:10,010
See this?

562
00:21:10,270 --> 00:21:10,600
Look.

563
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:13,650
Chen Jiahao,

564
00:21:14,550 --> 00:21:15,480
Shapu Village's

565
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:17,500
acting village chief.

566
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:18,970
Hello, Jiahao.

567
00:21:19,270 --> 00:21:20,550
Come on, follow me!

568
00:21:21,110 --> 00:21:22,710
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

569
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:27,510
The hometown of "King of Comedy"

570
00:21:27,510 --> 00:21:28,510
can be said to have

571
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:32,440
gathered all the wisdom
from the villagers of Shapu Village

572
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,160
and the leadership team.

573
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:35,270
We...

574
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:37,880
thought hard.

575
00:21:38,590 --> 00:21:40,400
We pooled everyone's wisdom

576
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:41,870
to come up with such...

577
00:21:42,590 --> 00:21:43,310
a good...

578
00:21:46,030 --> 00:21:46,640
idea.

579
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:50,480
And these tourists were just...

580
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,730
dragged off halfway by you.

581
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,440
Regarding your idea,

582
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,620
I have three points to make.

583
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,590
Three points?

584
00:21:57,750 --> 00:21:59,790
What I just said was my first point!

585
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:01,590
-Great!
-Great!

586
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:03,440
-Great!
-Great!

587
00:22:04,910 --> 00:22:06,510
What about the second point?

588
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:08,920
The second point.

589
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:17,300
Why did you park the bus
in the middle of the road?

590
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:18,790
T-This is the second point?

591
00:22:18,790 --> 00:22:20,030
Okay, I'll move it later.

592
00:22:20,030 --> 00:22:21,490
Come on, let's go this way!

593
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:22,590
I remembered the second point!

594
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:24,320
I remembered the second point!

595
00:22:24,590 --> 00:22:25,120
These...

596
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:26,480
passengers

597
00:22:26,510 --> 00:22:28,840
were clearly heading for Shapu Village.

598
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,550
But you stopped them halfway.

599
00:22:30,550 --> 00:22:31,400
Is this...

600
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:32,350
okay?

601
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:33,440
No.

602
00:22:34,110 --> 00:22:34,510
No!

603
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:36,070
No, this is not okay!

604
00:22:36,750 --> 00:22:37,880
It's unreasonable!

605
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,730
What's the third point?

606
00:22:43,270 --> 00:22:44,440
Stop wasting time with them!

607
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,960
Let's just escort the bus back!

608
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,000
This is our bus!

609
00:22:55,550 --> 00:22:56,270
Stop it!

610
00:22:57,110 --> 00:22:57,720
Be reasonable!

611
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:59,450
Why were you getting physical?

612
00:23:01,350 --> 00:23:02,950
Where is your village chief?

613
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:08,970
I'm asking you.
Where is your village chief?

614
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:12,880
I am.

615
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,340
The acting one.

616
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:18,310
We meet at the top.

617
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:23,220
Acting village chief, right?

618
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
So you led your villagers

619
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,130
to make trouble in our village, right?

620
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,240
You guys were in the wrong first.

621
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:32,480
We were the ones who made
the hometown of "King of Comedy"

622
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,310
popular.

623
00:23:33,310 --> 00:23:34,400
You just took the credit

624
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:36,790
and claimed Chuanao
is the hometown of "King of Comedy."

625
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:38,200
This is false marketing.

626
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,200
Be polite.

627
00:23:39,510 --> 00:23:41,400
Stephen Chow's "King of Comedy"

628
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:43,350
was filmed in both of our villages.

629
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:44,590
The line "Work harder! Keep on!"

630
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:46,720
was filmed on the sea near our village.

631
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,680
We didn't do false marketing, did we?

632
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,750
Then what about you using
your geographical advantage

633
00:23:50,750 --> 00:23:52,750
to intercept our tourists halfway?

634
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:54,840
Intercept tourists?

635
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:01,070
I think there must be a misunderstanding.

636
00:24:01,070 --> 00:24:03,270
I will investigate it thoroughly
when I get back

637
00:24:03,270 --> 00:24:04,920
and give everyone an explanation.

638
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,580
But I, Fang Hua, am here today.

639
00:24:06,790 --> 00:24:07,960
I promise you

640
00:24:08,310 --> 00:24:10,510
that this will never happen again.

641
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,160
But as for which village
the tourists go to in the future,

642
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,350
let's rely on our own abilities

643
00:24:15,350 --> 00:24:16,110
and compete fairly.

644
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:16,510
Great!

645
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:19,000
Fair competition.

646
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,200
It's settled today.

647
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:21,830
Settled what?

648
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,680
What about this bus full of tourists?

649
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:25,200
Yeah, what about these tourists?
What should we do?

650
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,000
Stop arguing!

651
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:28,160
Then what about these tourists?

652
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,620
You can take the tourists.

653
00:24:29,750 --> 00:24:31,150
You can keep half of them.

654
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:33,000
Keep what? Take them away.

655
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,000
We'll take them...

656
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,550
Shapu Village is still
the hometown of "King of Comedy."

657
00:24:36,550 --> 00:24:38,010
Let's get on the bus first.

658
00:24:43,270 --> 00:24:44,530
Who told you to do this?

659
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:47,920
Me.

660
00:24:54,750 --> 00:24:57,160
I told you to pick up
tourists at the station,

661
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,710
not to intercept them.

662
00:24:58,730 --> 00:24:59,590
What do you mean?

663
00:24:59,590 --> 00:25:00,520
I have an accent?

664
00:25:01,270 --> 00:25:02,110
I'm sorry, Ms. Ma.

665
00:25:02,110 --> 00:25:02,910
Sorry to whom?

666
00:25:03,510 --> 00:25:04,570
Sorry, Chief Fang.

667
00:25:04,790 --> 00:25:07,920
Chief Fang, today's incident
is really a misunderstanding.

668
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:08,650
I apologize.

669
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:10,830
Yes.

670
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:13,200
Ms. Ma just came to our village.

671
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:15,050
She doesn't know much

672
00:25:15,350 --> 00:25:16,790
about our situation, right?

673
00:25:16,790 --> 00:25:17,680
No, she doesn't know,

674
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:18,790
but don't you know?

675
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:22,450
Fortunately,
a fight didn't break out today.

676
00:25:24,750 --> 00:25:25,310
Ms. Ma,

677
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:26,890
you have no idea.

678
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,350
Before the founding of the PRC,

679
00:25:28,350 --> 00:25:30,350
many people died or were injured
in armed conflicts

680
00:25:30,350 --> 00:25:33,280
between the two villages
over a little bit of profit.

681
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,830
My third granduncle's fourth granduncle

682
00:25:34,830 --> 00:25:36,490
died in battle just like that.

683
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:38,640
Chief Fang,

684
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,970
please accept my condolences.

685
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:42,400
But regarding today's incident,

686
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:44,200
I failed to discipline my subordinates.

687
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:44,920
I know.

688
00:25:44,920 --> 00:25:45,920
I promise you,

689
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:47,440
it will never happen again.

690
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:48,640
Ms. Ma already knows.

691
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:49,640
Chief Fang, we should just...

692
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:50,400
Know what?

693
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:52,530
You always think you know everything.

694
00:25:55,270 --> 00:25:55,720
Ms. Ma.

695
00:25:57,750 --> 00:25:59,440
I actually know exactly

696
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,970
why you came to our village.

697
00:26:01,110 --> 00:26:02,200
I don't care about that.

698
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:04,310
But if it affects the interests
of our villagers

699
00:26:04,310 --> 00:26:06,240
and the reputation of our village,

700
00:26:06,590 --> 00:26:08,350
that wouldn't be very good, would it?

701
00:26:08,350 --> 00:26:09,750
Yes, of course.

702
00:26:10,270 --> 00:26:10,930
Chief Fang,

703
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:12,590
we have to look at it this way.

704
00:26:12,590 --> 00:26:14,750
Chuanao Village has transformed
from a small fishing village

705
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:17,480
into the gold-medal tourist village
it is today.

706
00:26:18,030 --> 00:26:19,400
This, of course, couldn't have happened
without the joint efforts

707
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:21,400
of you and our Ma Group.

708
00:26:21,550 --> 00:26:25,000
I believe we will definitely
achieve mutual benefit in the future.

709
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:25,800
And what else?

710
00:26:25,830 --> 00:26:27,290
Move forward hand in hand.

711
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:46,590
Honey, I'm sorry.

712
00:26:46,590 --> 00:26:47,460
Did I hit you too hard just now?

713
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:48,110
Let me rub it.

714
00:26:48,110 --> 00:26:48,710
Come here.

715
00:26:49,590 --> 00:26:50,030
I'm sorry.

716
00:26:50,030 --> 00:26:51,270
You hit this side.

717
00:26:51,270 --> 00:26:51,870
This side?

718
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:52,920
I'm sorry.

719
00:26:52,950 --> 00:26:54,150
-Be good.
-It's okay.

720
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:55,030
Honey.

721
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,160
How dare a mere village chief

722
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:58,310
talk to you like that?

723
00:26:58,310 --> 00:26:59,000
I'm so mad.

724
00:26:59,000 --> 00:26:59,680
Exactly.

725
00:26:59,790 --> 00:27:01,680
Even my dad wouldn't dare talk to me
like that.

726
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,540
How about this?

727
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:04,310
You should quickly tell your dad

728
00:27:04,310 --> 00:27:05,590
about our relationship.

729
00:27:05,590 --> 00:27:07,830
Otherwise, he'll always think
I'm just a driver,

730
00:27:07,830 --> 00:27:08,960
I-I'm a secretary,

731
00:27:09,110 --> 00:27:10,060
or I'm Mr. Liu.

732
00:27:10,110 --> 00:27:10,510
If you do that,

733
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:12,590
I can stand up for you legitimately.

734
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:13,320
Honey.

735
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:14,480
I'm so mad.

736
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:16,000
Let's wait a bit longer

737
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:18,150
until the time is right.

738
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:21,830
Honey,

739
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:24,420
if we hadn't been married
for almost 3 years,

740
00:27:25,070 --> 00:27:27,640
I would've definitely thought
you were a player.

741
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:28,200
I...

742
00:27:29,390 --> 00:27:30,870
Calm down.

743
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,680
Since they don't let us snatch tourists,

744
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:34,480
what should we do?

745
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:35,480
As for snatching,

746
00:27:36,470 --> 00:27:37,670
there are many kinds.

747
00:27:39,310 --> 00:27:40,310
Let's go, Mr. Liu.

748
00:27:40,350 --> 00:27:40,680
Wait.

749
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:42,640
Mr. Liu?

750
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:44,640
I'm used to calling you that, Honey.

751
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,790
From now on, when we are together,

752
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:48,000
you can't call me Mr. Liu

753
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,240
or Secretary Liu.

754
00:27:49,310 --> 00:27:50,000
What should you call me?

755
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:51,030
Honey?

756
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:54,510
Let's go. What do you want to eat?
My treat.

757
00:27:54,510 --> 00:27:56,000
I haven't eaten well since I came here.

758
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:56,440
How about this?

759
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:58,750
You treat me to a high-end Japanese meal.

760
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:03,550
Why do I suddenly want to eat

761
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:04,750
KFC's egg tarts?

762
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,240
K-KFC?

763
00:28:07,350 --> 00:28:07,960
They're pretty good.

764
00:28:07,960 --> 00:28:09,360
Today is Crazy Thursday.

765
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:10,000
Let's go.

766
00:28:17,160 --> 00:28:17,960
Is this right?

767
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:18,760
Is this right?

768
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:20,030
Why didn't you take us?

769
00:28:20,030 --> 00:28:21,240
Why didn't you take us?

770
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:22,440
If we had gone...

771
00:28:22,510 --> 00:28:24,110
Wouldn't the problem have been solved?

772
00:28:24,110 --> 00:28:24,790
Who am I?

773
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:26,440
Shapu's top tough guy!

774
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:28,040
Watch me sweep through them!

775
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:30,000
What is Chuanao anyway?

776
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:32,060
Then what were you two doing just now?

777
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:33,770
What were we doing? I...

778
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:37,310
Don't worry about what we were doing.

779
00:28:37,310 --> 00:28:38,790
Then why are you saying this in hindsight?

780
00:28:38,790 --> 00:28:39,070
Wait,

781
00:28:39,070 --> 00:28:40,750
did you get nothing out of it?

782
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:41,480
We did.

783
00:28:41,750 --> 00:28:42,270
What?

784
00:28:42,590 --> 00:28:43,830
Their village is doing better than ours.

785
00:28:43,830 --> 00:28:45,240
Do I need you to tell me that?

786
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,200
How good can it be?

787
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,060
Do they have...

788
00:28:47,550 --> 00:28:48,350
a convenience store?

789
00:28:48,350 --> 00:28:49,810
They have a shopping mall.

790
00:28:50,550 --> 00:28:52,110
Do they have a guesthouse
as good as ours?

791
00:28:52,110 --> 00:28:53,960
They have a hotel,
the Ocean Platinum Palace.

792
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:56,350
Do they have a dedicated tourist minibus

793
00:28:56,350 --> 00:28:58,110
from the county town to our Shapu?

794
00:28:58,110 --> 00:29:00,000
They have a high-speed rail station
right there.

795
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,480
Your minibus passed right by them.

796
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:02,310
How do you think
they intercepted the passengers?

797
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:03,200
That's how.

798
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:06,380
If we want to beat Chuanao now,

799
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:08,550
we need to find our village's advantages

800
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:10,410
and develop our unique features.

801
00:29:10,640 --> 00:29:11,240
So let's think about

802
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:12,270
what our village has

803
00:29:12,270 --> 00:29:13,870
that their village doesn't.

804
00:29:14,750 --> 00:29:16,000
Unique features.

805
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:18,880
What they don't have.

806
00:29:21,070 --> 00:29:22,440
Isn't it obvious?

807
00:29:23,350 --> 00:29:25,280
They don't have Shapu's tough guy.

808
00:29:26,830 --> 00:29:27,550
They don't.

809
00:29:27,750 --> 00:29:28,790
But it's useless.

810
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:33,840
There's also a soulless one.

811
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:34,920
When he saw the village chief just now,

812
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:36,160
his eyes almost popped out.

813
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:37,880
Jiahao, you really are...

814
00:29:40,240 --> 00:29:40,960
Alright.

815
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:42,290
Stop talking nonsense.

816
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:43,480
This is very simple.

817
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:45,000
I'll take the three Shapu kids

818
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,490
and go straight to their place.

819
00:29:46,490 --> 00:29:47,100
To do what?

820
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:47,680
What do you mean?

821
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:49,240
To snatch our tourists back.

822
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:49,590
Snatch them back.

823
00:29:49,590 --> 00:29:50,200
No, no.

824
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:53,000
I... I just talked to...

825
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:54,000
that chief.

826
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,400
We had a friendly negotiation.

827
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:57,920
We agreed that from now on, we will

828
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:58,880
compete fairly

829
00:29:59,790 --> 00:30:00,750
and develop peacefully.

830
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:01,640
If you go over there,

831
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:02,610
won't you just cause trouble for us?

832
00:30:02,610 --> 00:30:03,640
Who did you negotiate with?

833
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:05,310
Between us village chiefs.

834
00:30:05,330 --> 00:30:07,080
I... Do you understand me?

835
00:30:07,110 --> 00:30:08,110
This is all our...

836
00:30:08,110 --> 00:30:09,830
Alright, alright! Stop arguing!

837
00:30:09,830 --> 00:30:11,030
The leaders are...

838
00:30:13,510 --> 00:30:14,440
Let's eat first.

839
00:30:14,590 --> 00:30:15,960
We can think about it when we're full.

840
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:16,590
Honestly.

841
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:17,960
You don't know anything.

842
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:18,880
You haven't even picked your teeth clean.

843
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:19,810
What do you know?

844
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:23,690
Delicious.

845
00:30:24,750 --> 00:30:25,680
You... You're not allowed to eat.

846
00:30:25,680 --> 00:30:26,880
I'll give it to Ximei.

847
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:27,890
That's fine.

848
00:30:28,510 --> 00:30:29,170
Delicious.

849
00:30:30,790 --> 00:30:32,650
Don't... Don't move. Don't move.

850
00:30:36,190 --> 00:30:36,990
Wait a minute!

851
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:42,550
Zhen.

852
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:46,020
Are you the only one who knows
how to make these fish balls?

853
